1. The scarcity of good men: "For the godly man ceaseth," &c. There is neither piety nor fidelity among men. 

2. The great abundance of the wicked, the licentious times; the perfidiousness, hypocrisy, and dissimulation of the men among whom he lived. "They speak vanity every one with his neighbour," &c.;

